---
const images = [
  { src: "/images/category-safaris.avif", alt: "Safari vehicle crossing the savanna" },
  { src: "/images/lodge-siringit-camp.jpg", alt: "Comfortable lodge tent interior" },
  { src: "/images/why-travel-cheetah.jpg", alt: "Cheetah resting in golden grass" },
  { src: "/images/destination-kenya.jpg", alt: "Wildlife roaming the Kenyan plains" },
  { src: "/images/lodge-zuri-zanzibar.webp", alt: "Relaxed seating inside a safari vehicle" },
  { src: "/images/destination-tanzania.avif", alt: "Zebras grazing across the Tanzanian savanna" },
];
---

<section class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-20 md:mt-32 flex flex-col items-center px-4 sm:px-8">
  <h2 class="font-body font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl text-center leading-tight text-primary">
    How a Safari in East Africa with Atlas Safaris Works
  </h2>
  <div class="w-16 h-[3px] bg-primary mt-4 mb-8"></div>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 max-w-[820px]">
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      We organize safaris in East Africa's national parks and reserves, where wildlife can be
      observed in its natural habitat. Lions, leopards, elephants, giraffes, antelopes, and other
      savanna wildlife can often be seen just a few meters away.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      By evening, your safari guide will take you to a comfortable lodge, where you can enjoy
      dinner and relax. The next day, the journey continues with new animals and breathtaking
      landscapes. Thanks to the cool morning temperatures, savanna animals are especially active
      at dawn.
    </p>
    <p class="font-body text-base text-center leading-[162.5%] text-text">
      Time on safari is not limited to game drives in a 4x4 vehicle. Your vacation can be
      complemented with a hot-air balloon flight, visits to traditional tribes, or a guided walking
      safari. This is one of the few places on Earth that has remained almost unchanged for
      centuries.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 w-full mt-10">
    {
      images.map((image) => (
        <div class="h-48 sm:h-56 md:h-64 rounded-lg overflow-clip">
          <img src={image.src} alt={image.alt} class="size-full object-cover" />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
